WEBVTT

00:12.970 --> 00:18.710
Hikari ga sasu sora, umareochiru kage
In the bright sky illuminated by
sunlight, darkened shadows are born.

00:18.810 --> 00:24.150
Unmei wa dokomademo hikisakareru
Fate itself is being torn apart.

00:25.190 --> 00:30.150
Donna toki mo kesshite akiramenainara
If you never give up, no matter what happens,

00:30.330 --> 00:37.560
mada tozasareteru tobira kanarazu hiraku
Even that locked door will open for you.

00:38.530 --> 00:43.990
Eien datte dakishimete, fuuin mo tokihanachi
Embrace eternity and release the seal.

00:44.070 --> 00:49.940
Mamorubekimono ga ima kokoni wa arukara
Because the ones you wish
to protect are right here.

00:49.940 --> 00:55.880
Namida mo gyutto dakishimete,
yasashisa de tsutsumikomi
Embrace their tears with kindness.

00:55.880 --> 01:01.560
Nagareru mizu no youni tsuyoku nare
Become strong like the formless water,

01:01.560 --> 01:07.550
omouyouni tsuyoku nare
Become as strong as you wish to be.

01:07.700 --> 01:13.170
Mou jibun ni obienaide
Stop being afraid of yourself.

01:13.170 --> 01:19.800
Sou mirai wo osorenaide
Do not fear the future.

01:51.470 --> 01:53.070
When did you?!

02:05.150 --> 02:07.520
Hand over the Sakasaen.

02:08.260 --> 02:13.220
Our Fox Deity, Does a Grand Fight

02:19.830 --> 02:20.630
Dammit!

02:20.970 --> 02:21.700
What?!

02:26.540 --> 02:29.380
I really liked that one, too.

02:29.380 --> 02:31.140
Hey! Stop running away! Get back here!

02:36.780 --> 02:38.880
Eat him alive! Don't hesitate!

02:39.220 --> 02:40.350
Understood.

02:40.590 --> 02:43.320
Do you know who I am?

02:43.590 --> 02:46.220
What do you think this toy can do?

02:49.700 --> 02:52.930
Of all people, you're gonna insult puppets?

03:05.950 --> 03:07.180
You're such a fool...

03:16.190 --> 03:17.860
Fireworks at the park?

03:17.860 --> 03:22.900
Yup. We'll start at 7 tonight.
I'll bring all the stuff.

03:22.900 --> 03:27.870
Why the sudden plan, anyway?
Who else is coming?

03:27.870 --> 03:31.240
It'll be our lovable male badminton club members.

03:31.970 --> 03:33.170
And some others.

03:33.540 --> 03:36.030
Who are these others?

03:52.790 --> 03:54.090
Money...

04:14.580 --> 04:19.180
Don't get mad at me. It was just a little game.

04:19.690 --> 04:24.020
Think of it as a lucky 5 yen coin
that gave birth to a new friendship.

04:24.460 --> 04:26.390
That's a 50 yen coin.

04:26.390 --> 04:30.520
What? Really?! Shoot.

04:31.400 --> 04:34.440
Well, whatever. Doesn't really matter.

04:34.440 --> 04:36.900
Anyway, Mamorime of the Mizuchi.

04:38.310 --> 04:42.280
I have some business with the
head of the Mizuchi family.

04:42.280 --> 04:43.970
I need your help.

04:46.080 --> 04:47.380
Go away!

04:47.620 --> 04:49.220
What's with you all of a sudden?

04:49.220 --> 04:51.420
How did you find out where I live?!

04:51.420 --> 04:54.460
Did you follow me here?

04:54.460 --> 04:56.560
I get it! You're stalking me!

04:56.560 --> 04:58.530
You don't have to get so nasty...

04:58.530 --> 05:01.860
I asked the hashihime of the
Hashiba Shrine for this location.

05:01.860 --> 05:03.260
Who's that?

05:03.260 --> 05:06.000
The hashihime is the brethren of the presiding god.

05:06.000 --> 05:10.730
If she told him of this place,
I doubt he's dangerous.

05:10.910 --> 05:12.770
Are you sure?

05:12.770 --> 05:16.310
We just went through so much
trouble because of that raccoon dog.

05:16.310 --> 05:19.480
I don't play tricks on people like raccoon dogs.

05:19.480 --> 05:21.410
Not very convincing, coming from a raccoon dog.

05:21.480 --> 05:24.920
Wait, raccoon dog? Don't tell me you...

05:25.690 --> 05:30.120
This isn't a raccoon dog mask.
It's supposed to be an owl.

05:35.400 --> 05:36.120
It's a raccoon dog!

05:42.870 --> 05:43.840
Here you go.

05:44.140 --> 05:45.730
Thank you.

05:46.010 --> 05:47.240
Oh yes...

05:47.510 --> 05:49.340
This may not be much, but...

05:49.510 --> 05:52.550
Wow! Salted salmon cookies!

05:52.550 --> 05:55.280
Oh, you didn't have to...

05:55.420 --> 05:56.820
Is it to your liking?

05:57.090 --> 05:59.610
Then I'm glad I brought them.
Go ahead and take it.

05:59.790 --> 06:01.390
What's this?

06:01.390 --> 06:05.160
It's a kind of snack.
It's sweet, and salty, and really good!

06:05.160 --> 06:07.830
Oh? Let's try it.

06:07.830 --> 06:10.100
So what is it you wanted with me?

06:10.100 --> 06:14.160
Well, I am actually the presiding
deity of a certain land.

06:14.270 --> 06:16.900
Oh. You're also a god?

06:17.270 --> 06:19.360
Which land are you god of?

06:20.380 --> 06:21.780
Salted Salmon Cookies

06:21.780 --> 06:22.970
Salted Salmon Cookies
Oh...

06:23.310 --> 06:29.110
I wanted to talk to you about the
treasure of my land, the Sakasaen.

06:35.460 --> 06:38.390
That Sugino!

06:38.390 --> 06:42.100
Why doesn't he tell me earlier
we're doing a get-together?

06:42.100 --> 06:43.830
Oh, geez!

06:44.370 --> 06:45.600
You got a minute?

06:45.600 --> 06:49.300
What is it this time? Why are you
hanging around in your underwear again.

06:49.570 --> 06:51.770
I was thinking about what to wear.

06:51.770 --> 06:52.570
Where're you going?

06:52.570 --> 06:55.880
Going to see fireworks!
I'm going to make my move today!

06:55.880 --> 07:00.540
You could even say the lasting memories
of the summer will depend on this!

07:00.620 --> 07:03.520
There's one thing you can always
wear for summer fireworks.

07:03.920 --> 07:05.040
What's that?

07:07.020 --> 07:11.920
Anyway, that was how the Sakasaen
was stolen by a drifter yokai.

07:12.830 --> 07:16.820
I heard it was later found
somewhere near this area.

07:20.170 --> 07:22.930
I heard the Sakasaen always belonged to Mubyo.

07:23.170 --> 07:28.070
That's not true. I swear to you
that the Sakasaen belongs to me.

07:34.120 --> 07:37.450
Feeling...

07:38.050 --> 07:41.890
Kinda...

07:41.890 --> 07:43.950
That's great!

07:44.030 --> 07:45.080
Yeah!

07:45.530 --> 07:49.290
I'm the only one in the 4th grade
who got picked as one of the players!

07:49.400 --> 07:52.830
Oh, really? Good job.

07:55.940 --> 07:58.630
Happy...

07:59.810 --> 08:05.710
Mubyo only says it is hers because
it happened to fall into her hands.

08:06.780 --> 08:10.650
Last night, I tried to convince her to give it back.

08:11.250 --> 08:16.160
She ignored me and fled to Suzunose.

08:16.390 --> 08:20.830
She's more of a trickster than I thought.

08:25.870 --> 08:28.930
Thank goodness...

08:29.540 --> 08:32.940
Mubyo-chan was lying?

08:36.210 --> 08:40.920
Tenko. I heard you assisted in
returning the Sakasaen to her.

08:40.920 --> 08:42.250
Yes...

08:42.520 --> 08:46.590
Then think of our encounter as
fate and help me find Mubyo.

08:46.590 --> 08:47.760
What?

08:47.760 --> 08:50.950
Noboru-kun, can you try to
talk to the tenko for me?

08:51.230 --> 08:53.130
At least to thank me for this gift.

08:53.490 --> 08:56.790
I guess so. We did already eat it...

08:58.300 --> 08:59.930
It's such a pain in the ass!

08:59.930 --> 09:03.300
Let's go, Ku-chan! I'll go with you.

09:06.910 --> 09:10.240
Thank you, Toru-kun. You have my thanks.

09:14.250 --> 09:18.380
Why does everyone run to Suzunose
whenever something happens?!

09:19.290 --> 09:20.310
Welcome.

09:21.460 --> 09:23.460
Can I ask you something?

09:23.460 --> 09:24.820
S-Sure!

09:25.160 --> 09:31.330
Did you recently see a woman wearing a
coat with sheep and wolf hand puppets?

09:31.330 --> 09:36.430
Um... Um... I'm sorry.
I didn't see anyone like that.

09:38.440 --> 09:40.980
Seems like she didn't come around here.

09:40.980 --> 09:43.310
All right. Next.

09:46.810 --> 09:51.250
Why do all the problems always come to me?!

09:51.720 --> 09:53.020
Excuse me...

09:53.020 --> 09:53.780
Yes?

09:53.850 --> 09:59.490
I'm sorry for bothering you,
but may I ask you something?

09:59.630 --> 10:02.900
S-Sure! You can ask me anything!

10:02.900 --> 10:04.230
That's wonderful!

10:04.900 --> 10:07.300
Well, this is just great!

10:07.640 --> 10:08.840
How was it?

10:08.840 --> 10:09.890
He doesn't know anything.

10:10.140 --> 10:11.070
Oh...

10:11.370 --> 10:13.980
She's harder to find than I thought.

10:13.980 --> 10:15.940
You're right about that...

10:16.380 --> 10:18.970
Wait! There's something wrong here!

10:19.110 --> 10:23.850
Why am I doing all the work?! Stop slacking off!

10:24.090 --> 10:26.750
There, there. Let's go to the next one.

10:30.090 --> 10:31.230
Ku-chan.

10:31.230 --> 10:33.420
I'm not going to help you anymore!

10:34.660 --> 10:36.530
You want to go with me?

10:36.830 --> 10:38.730
I have a bad feeling about this...

10:38.730 --> 10:40.740
About what?

10:40.740 --> 10:41.900
I don't know yet.

10:41.900 --> 10:42.870
Oh...

10:45.210 --> 10:49.700
It's just gonna be guys there,
so it won't be any fun for you.

10:51.450 --> 10:52.710
I want to go.

11:02.060 --> 11:04.050
This is Ebisu's home...

11:04.790 --> 11:07.260
I highly doubt Mubyo will be...

11:07.800 --> 11:09.730
But something doesn't seem right.

11:09.730 --> 11:12.460
Hey, fox. Go up there and look around.

11:15.140 --> 11:16.140
Ku-chan...

11:16.140 --> 11:17.600
What are you doing? Hurry it up!

11:20.570 --> 11:24.750
Ku-chan! You could've hurt him!
What are you doing?

11:24.750 --> 11:26.880
Who do you think you are, bossing me around?!

11:26.880 --> 11:29.420
If you want to find her, go look for yourself!

11:29.420 --> 11:31.320
Just do as I say...

11:31.690 --> 11:35.120
You said you'd slave away for me, didn't you?

11:35.120 --> 11:38.420
What?! When did I say that?!

11:38.930 --> 11:42.260
I suppose lowly beasts like
you have a terrible memory.

11:44.170 --> 11:45.630
Fine...

11:46.070 --> 11:50.940
I'll erase you and then forget you ever existed!

12:01.520 --> 12:03.180
This thing isn't...

12:08.290 --> 12:11.260
He's doing this now?

12:13.360 --> 12:16.450
How long will he keep toying with me?

12:31.250 --> 12:33.480
I'm so happy I got to see you again!

12:33.480 --> 12:35.470
You look awesome in that
shrine maiden outfit, as always!

12:36.620 --> 12:38.820
Your name was Ko-san, right?

12:38.820 --> 12:41.410
Is it true you live with Noboru?

12:41.660 --> 12:43.820
She's that kimono girl everyone's talking about...

12:43.820 --> 12:44.990
- She's so cute.

12:44.990 --> 12:45.790
- Hey!
- She's so cute.

12:45.790 --> 12:47.190
What are you doing?!

12:47.900 --> 12:49.590
Stop bothering her!

12:49.900 --> 12:52.430
Wait, I thought only the guys were coming today.

12:52.430 --> 12:54.460
I told you there were going to be others, didn't I?

12:54.870 --> 12:58.100
Geez, you can be dense when
in comes to these things.

12:58.810 --> 13:00.840
Haven't seen you in a while, Ko-chan.

13:00.840 --> 13:01.500
Yes.

13:02.010 --> 13:04.670
So you're wearing a yukata today!

13:06.350 --> 13:08.320
You look great in it...

13:09.120 --> 13:10.380
Really?

13:12.050 --> 13:13.520
Y-Yeah.

13:13.920 --> 13:15.180
Thanks...

13:16.090 --> 13:17.420
Dense little bastard.

13:22.400 --> 13:25.520
I'll turn this owl into barbecued fowl!

13:26.370 --> 13:28.270
Good. Do some more damage.

13:35.480 --> 13:38.010
Keep this on you no matter what!

13:38.010 --> 13:40.920
I'll end things with that birdbrain right now.

13:40.920 --> 13:42.470
Are you really going to fight him?

13:42.680 --> 13:45.550
He's looking for a fight. I'm just giving it to him.

13:45.550 --> 13:48.890
Fukuro-san, why would you
taunt her like that anyway?

13:48.890 --> 13:51.220
What about the search for Mubyo-chan?

13:51.560 --> 13:54.620
The search for Mubyo will end very soon.

13:56.130 --> 13:58.330
Why does it always end up like this?

13:58.970 --> 14:02.490
Idiots like you need to be taught a lesson.

14:03.900 --> 14:05.930
You're the one that'll be given a lesson!

14:06.940 --> 14:07.870
What?!

14:08.840 --> 14:09.870
What is this?!

14:10.110 --> 14:11.850
You can't move now, can you?

14:11.850 --> 14:12.640
Damn this!

14:13.150 --> 14:14.080
It's no use.

14:21.760 --> 14:23.120
I said it's no use.

14:23.260 --> 14:25.190
Do you really think so?

14:26.030 --> 14:27.020
What?!

14:27.760 --> 14:29.660
Looks like you were wrong.

14:37.810 --> 14:39.900
That's enough!

14:50.180 --> 14:52.690
All right! I'm next!

14:52.690 --> 14:53.710
Good luck!

15:00.130 --> 15:01.560
It's beautiful...

15:02.360 --> 15:05.330
All right. Me next!

15:05.330 --> 15:06.870
You're starting to get into it.

15:06.870 --> 15:08.030
Give us a big one!

15:20.810 --> 15:21.750
All right!

15:24.390 --> 15:27.220
I didn't know Takagami had such a boyish side...

15:27.490 --> 15:29.510
I think I just found another thing I like about him.

15:34.860 --> 15:37.530
Don't you get thirsty from eating so much of that?

15:37.530 --> 15:39.690
Want me to get you something to drink?

15:40.100 --> 15:42.030
This amount of thirst is nothing.

15:42.740 --> 15:43.770
I can put up with it.

15:43.770 --> 15:45.830
You don't have to...

15:46.710 --> 15:49.870
By the way, well...

15:50.210 --> 15:54.010
Do you talk to Takagami a lot at home?

15:54.380 --> 15:55.910
If I'm ordered to do so.

15:57.920 --> 16:00.510
I guess you do seem pretty old-fashioned...

16:00.890 --> 16:03.120
Like being a good wife and
wise mother type of thing...

16:10.060 --> 16:12.730
Wait, no!

16:12.730 --> 16:17.360
Does Takagami ever talk about me?

16:17.670 --> 16:19.970
So that was the source of the ill omen I felt.

16:26.310 --> 16:30.220
I mess up on the job and then
get dumped by my girlfriend...

16:30.550 --> 16:32.680
This sucks, yo...

16:33.390 --> 16:35.560
Am I cursed or something?

16:35.560 --> 16:36.520
It would seem so.

16:41.860 --> 16:44.060
Wh-What are you doing?!

16:44.060 --> 16:46.500
You're going a bit too far with your prank!

16:47.000 --> 16:49.560
I exorcised the spirit possessing you.

16:50.970 --> 16:52.070
Now that you mention it...

16:52.070 --> 16:55.270
I feel like a weight got
unloaded from my shoulders...

16:55.780 --> 16:58.850
Like something bad inside me just melted away...

16:58.850 --> 16:59.980
You serious?

16:59.980 --> 17:02.920
Hey, look. She's actually a shrine maiden.

17:05.190 --> 17:10.890
Thank you, mysterious shrine maiden!
Here, take anything you want!

17:17.800 --> 17:19.860
Laters! Thanks again!

17:20.470 --> 17:23.490
Ko-chan, why did you go off all of a sudden?

17:27.370 --> 17:29.470
Are you okay, Ko-chan?

17:30.940 --> 17:34.400
So... funny!

17:37.580 --> 17:39.140
H-Hey!

17:40.550 --> 17:43.180
Stop breaking things in my territory!

17:43.990 --> 17:46.890
The condition of the land is bad enough as it is!

17:57.640 --> 18:01.310
Please! Anything but the power lines!

18:01.310 --> 18:02.570
I beg of you!

18:03.040 --> 18:05.530
Oh, right. I forgot about that.

18:18.860 --> 18:22.320
So this is like holding a party by the Amano-Iwato?

18:22.660 --> 18:24.220
I won't let you have your way!

18:35.510 --> 18:37.940
There's no end to this!

18:40.650 --> 18:45.280
I'll kill you... I'll kill you idiots...

18:45.650 --> 18:47.310
I'll kill all of you!

18:56.860 --> 19:00.900
Why would you summon miasma into
your own land? Have you gone mad?

19:00.900 --> 19:04.030
I don't wanna hear that from
someone who cut the power lines!

19:05.270 --> 19:08.400
Manifested Earth-2. Primordial Earth-5.
Manifested Earth-5. Primordial Earth-8.

19:21.860 --> 19:22.980
What is this?!

19:26.330 --> 19:27.420
She's here...

19:29.000 --> 19:31.560
How long are they going to keep that up?

19:32.300 --> 19:35.390
There's a show I wanna watch,
so maybe I should just go home.

19:41.410 --> 19:42.710
Mubyo-chan!

19:42.980 --> 19:47.640
Yoo-hoo! Hiya! It's been like, a day since we met!

19:50.880 --> 19:52.320
Pitiful.

19:52.320 --> 19:53.050
What?!

19:53.750 --> 19:56.020
Let's stop this fight, you two.

19:56.390 --> 19:57.820
I'm sorry.

19:58.060 --> 20:00.290
Allow me to speak a few words of apology...

20:01.030 --> 20:02.220
So for now, let's...

20:05.830 --> 20:08.360
All right! Striiiike!

20:08.870 --> 20:11.630
We were looking for you, Mubyo-chan.

20:11.970 --> 20:13.870
Yeah, I know.

20:14.410 --> 20:18.610
That owl face probably told you
I stole the Sakasaen from him.

20:20.480 --> 20:22.240
Toru-chan, do you believe him?

20:26.590 --> 20:28.110
So you do.

20:32.730 --> 20:36.030
There's no proof that what he said is true.

20:36.030 --> 20:39.000
But you don't have proof that
the Sakasaen is yours either!

20:39.630 --> 20:41.830
That's a really roundabout way to spin it.

20:44.370 --> 20:45.360
I'm sorry.

20:48.380 --> 20:53.640
It's all right. I know you're
trying your best not to hurt me.

20:54.150 --> 20:55.110
Thanks...

20:57.020 --> 20:58.880
You're such a good boy...

20:59.590 --> 21:01.080
And smart, too.

21:02.290 --> 21:03.290
Mubyo-chan.

21:03.290 --> 21:04.020
Yeah?

21:04.390 --> 21:05.980
Who does the Sakasaen belong to?

21:09.300 --> 21:11.060
You ARE smart...

21:12.300 --> 21:16.170
Well... I don't know who it belongs to either.

21:19.470 --> 21:24.980
Anyway, I lost my contacts somewhere over there!

21:24.980 --> 21:26.950
Can you help me look for it?

21:30.020 --> 21:30.880
Sure.

21:33.190 --> 21:34.210
Thanks!

21:44.400 --> 21:50.860
Sora no hate ga tsunagaru basho wo
Where the horizon meets the earth,

21:51.340 --> 21:58.540
no ni saku hana wa mada kitto shiranai
The flower growing in the wild remains unaware.

21:59.910 --> 22:06.410
Kokoyori ii sekai ga aruto
While thinking that there
is a world better than this.

22:06.550 --> 22:14.190
Kokoro wa itsumo hane wo hirogetagaru
They always desire to spread
the wings of their hearts.

22:15.100 --> 22:22.130
Yume dakede owarasenai
Don't let it end as just a dream,

22:22.740 --> 22:29.230
chansu ga aru hazusa
There's always a chance.

22:29.440 --> 22:36.880
Daijoubu bokura wa hitori janai
It's all right. We are not alone.

22:36.880 --> 22:44.490
Kaze ga nanika wo iouto shiteru
The winds are telling us something.

22:44.490 --> 22:52.170
Daijoubu kanarazu umaku yareru
It's all right. You can do it.

22:52.170 --> 23:03.410
Omoi wa itsuka jibun wo kaeru michi ni naru
Those dreams are a path you'll change yourself.

23:15.860 --> 23:16.850
You're...

23:17.020 --> 23:18.350
It can't be...

23:21.630 --> 23:22.750
Mubyo...

23:25.000 --> 23:25.900
Next Time

23:25.900 --> 23:28.140
Next Time
The heart always yearns for something.

23:28.140 --> 23:31.100
Next Time
And yet words betray the heart at times.

23:31.100 --> 23:31.340
Next Time

23:31.340 --> 23:33.910
Next Time
You have to understand what you can't see.

23:33.910 --> 23:34.110
Next Time

23:34.110 --> 23:35.110
Next Time
Next time, "Our Fox Deity, Betrays?!"

23:35.110 --> 23:36.610
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Betrays?!
Next time, "Our Fox Deity, Betrays?!"

23:36.610 --> 23:36.880
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Betrays?!

23:36.880 --> 23:39.450
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Betrays?!
Is this what they call the
whimsical heart of a maiden?!

23:39.450 --> 23:39.970
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Betrays?!
